323 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 54 0 R
/E (Testing was an essential part of evaluating the performance of our JAF Racing Team car. Once the main components had been assembled, we tested the vehicle on the track to observe how it performed under the conditions available to us. Our main objective was to evaluate its movement, speed, and stability and determine whether the final configuration met our expectations.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [22]
>>
endobj
324 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 54 0 R
/E (After reviewing the results of our tests, we were satisfied with the speed and stability we observed. We therefore decided to maintain the overall configuration of the car instead of making additional changes to its main structure. This decision was based on our evaluation of the performance achieved during the tests and our satisfaction with the results.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [23]
>>
endobj
325 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 54 0 R
/E (Although we did not introduce further changes to the overall configuration after testing, the evaluation stage remained important because it gave us the opportunity to confirm that the car behaved as expected. It also helped us develop a better understanding of the relationship between the design choices we made and the performance of the completed vehicle.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [24]
>>
endobj
